# .NET Backend

- Target `net10.0`, keep nullable and implicit usings on.
- Controllers/Minimal APIs only orchestrate; call Application use cases.
- Register dependencies in composition root; no service locator.
- Use async APIs end-to-end with `CancellationToken`.
- Validation belongs at Application boundary (FluentValidation or equivalent), not buried in controllers.
- Prefer explicit DTOs for request/response contracts.
- Keep Domain free of EF Core, ASP.NET, and HTTP types.
- Infrastructure owns `DbContext`, migrations, and external integrations.
- Prefer Central Package Management (`Directory.Packages.props`) for multi-project solutions.
- Use `Directory.Build.props` for shared build settings across solution projects.
- Structured logging only; never log secrets or full PII.
- After meaningful backend changes, run `dotnet build` and relevant `dotnet test`.
